## 6. How it renders (no change needed)

`src/config/appComponentsMap.js` maps the **tasks** tab to `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue`, which already switches on `activeBoard.type === 'sprint'`:

```js appComponentsMap.js (existing)
'tasks': KanbanBoardView,
```
```js KanbanBoardView.vue (existing, unchanged)
isSprintBoard() {
  return this.activeBoard?.type === 'sprint'
}
```

Because the virtual board is `type: 'sprint'`, selecting the **"No board"** card routes straight into `SprintBoardView` and renders the orphan chats across the status columns — **zero changes to the composition root**.

---

## 7. Accessibility Checklist
- ✅ Virtual card uses an **icon + text badge** ("no board") — meaning is never colour-only.
- ✅ Bookmark toggle is **hidden** for the virtual board (no dead interactive control).
- ✅ Icon-only buttons keep `title` / `aria-label` (inherited from sprint internals).
- ✅ Read-only state removes creation affordances instead of disabling them without explanation; a visible "chats without a board" hint explains the mode.
- ✅ Drag-between-status remains available (keyboard-less drag is an existing limitation of the sprint board).
- ⚠️ **Follow-up (out of scope):** `SprintTaskCard.vue` still renders its per-card "Remove from sprint" button; on the virtual board this now maps to a guarded no-op. Hide it there (`v-if="!virtual"`) when that file is touched.

## 8. Anti-Patterns avoided
- ❌ Persisting the virtual board (it is synthesised on read — no writes, no `kanban.boards` pollution).
- ❌ Letting the virtual board appear in the sprint switcher / parent-board selector (excluded).
- ❌ Creating tasks with a bogus `sprints: ['No board']` membership (guarded + UI hidden).

